      "GENERAL NOTE: This Figure illustrates the nomenclature of para. 304.3.3. It does not indicate complete welding details of a preferred method of construction. For typical welding details, see Figures 328.5.4-2 and 328.5.4-4.",
      "(1) When a reinforcing ring or saddle is added as reinforcement (Example A and Detail for Example A), the value of reinforcement area may be taken in the same manner in which excess wall in run pipe, A2, is considered. Typical acceptable methods of welding are shown in Figure 328.5.4-2, illustrations (c) through (e).",
      "(2) Width-to-height of reinforcing ring or saddle area A4 shall be reasonably proportioned, preferably on a ratio as close to 4:1 as the available horizontal space within the limits of the reinforcing zone along the run and the outside diameter of the branch will permit, but in no case may the ratio be less than 1:1.",
      "(3) Reinforcing saddles are limited to use on 90-deg branches (detail for Example A).",
      "(4) This 60-deg angle is not a limit on the angle of the integral nozzle geometry. The 60-deg angle defines the line that is used to set the height of reinforcement, Tr. The full area below the height of reinforcement can be accounted for in calculating the reinforcement area, A4. A4 is the added metal within the reinforcement zone excluding the excess metal in the run pipe, A2, and the excess metal in the branch pipe, A3."
